---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Insights"
  description="Ryan Laird's insights: essays on this site, research and writing, sector perspectives on space, Earth observation and sustainability, and the Signal & Noise newsletter."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="sl">Insights</p>

      <h1>Four places to read, one for how you like to read</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        I publish in different places because the work is different. Essays and notes live on this
        site, research and articles for other publications sit under research, sector pages gather
        what I know about each field, and the newsletter is where I check claims and add opinion.
        Pick the route that fits and you'll land on the right page.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="route-grid">
      <article class="route" id="blog" data-tone="teal">
        <h2>Blog</h2>
        <p>Essays and commentary published on this site: space strategy, science communication, sustainability and digital practice.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> readers who want the considered, longer view and a piece they can link to and come back to.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/insights/blog/">Read the blog</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" id="research" data-tone="violet">
        <h2>Research and writing</h2>
        <p>Research outputs and articles written for other publications, filterable by topic and by publication.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> researchers, editors, students and anyone checking what I've published elsewhere.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/research/">Research and writing</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" id="sectors" data-tone="sky">
        <h2>Sectors</h2>
        <p>Perspectives organised by field, so you can start from your own area rather than from a format.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> people in space, Earth observation, climate and sustainability, and deep tech who want the material that applies to them.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/work/sectors/">Browse the sectors</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" id="newsletter" data-tone="amber">
        <h2>Signal &amp; Noise newsletter</h2>
        <p>Space strategy, science communication and fact-checks when evidence loses to noise. New posts every week or two, with shorter Notes in between.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> readers who want the sourcing, not just the take.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/insights/substack/">About the newsletter</a>
        <a
          class="go"
          href="https://rjmlaird.substack.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Subscribe on Substack
          <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="block">
      <h2>Not sure where to start?</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        For a first read, the <a href="/insights/blog/">blog</a> is the best place. If you'd rather
        have things delivered, <a href="https://rjmlaird.substack.com/">subscribe to Signal &amp; Noise</a>.
        Looking for something specific, such as a topic, a publication or a sector? Try the
        filters on <a href="/research/">research and writing</a>, or
        <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> and I'll point you to it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>